1
00:00:27,632 --> 00:00:30,093
-All good?
-Checks are complete.

2
00:00:51,239 --> 00:00:54,075
IMMIGRATION OFFICER (MINISTRY OF JUSTICE)
KEIICHIRO HAYAMI

3
00:00:56,077 --> 00:00:58,705
CUSTOMS OFFICER (MINISTRY OF FINANCE)
ATSUSHI MATSUYAMA

4
00:00:58,788 --> 00:01:03,251
Creatine, approved. Zinc, approved.

5
00:01:03,334 --> 00:01:06,087
Melatonin, requires confirmation.

6
00:01:06,171 --> 00:01:09,174
Glutamine, approved,
assuming it matches the label.

7
00:01:09,257 --> 00:01:12,844
They're just regular supplements!
There's nothing suspicious here!

8
00:01:13,970 --> 00:01:15,805
In Japan, these are
pharmaceutical products,

9
00:01:15,889 --> 00:01:17,682
not general dietary supplements.

10
00:01:17,765 --> 00:01:20,476
They require a prescription
or fall under strict quantity limits.

11
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:22,770
Any personal supply
exceeding a two-month limit must--

12
00:01:22,854 --> 00:01:24,314
Just hurry it up already!

13
00:01:24,397 --> 00:01:25,273
What is she doing?

14
00:01:28,109 --> 00:01:30,069
It's the rules.

15
00:01:30,153 --> 00:01:32,322
You have a lot of these pills as well.

16
00:01:32,405 --> 00:01:34,866
There are barely any!

17
00:01:35,992 --> 00:01:39,537
Foreign visitors in Japan have more
than doubled over the last ten years.

18
00:01:39,621 --> 00:01:42,332
Over 40 million visited last year.

19
00:01:42,415 --> 00:01:44,959
<i>We are, however,</i>
<i>nearing our limit at the front lines.</i>

20
00:01:45,043 --> 00:01:47,086
<i>The problem lies</i>
<i>with the airport's structure itself.</i>

21
00:01:48,546 --> 00:01:50,632
Immigration is handled
by the Ministry of Justice,

22
00:01:50,715 --> 00:01:52,383
Customs by the Ministry of Finance,

23
00:01:52,467 --> 00:01:55,136
Quarantine by the Ministry of Health,

24
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:58,139
and the airport police by the National
Police Agency. Furthermore,

25
00:01:58,806 --> 00:02:00,850
there is the Ministry of Land,
the Ministry of Foreign Affairs,

26
00:02:00,934 --> 00:02:02,060
the Ministry of Defense,

27
00:02:02,143 --> 00:02:03,603
the Digital Agency…

28
00:02:04,187 --> 00:02:06,648
Airports are often called
a melting pot of races,

29
00:02:06,731 --> 00:02:08,650
but they are also a melting pot
of government offices.

30
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:09,567
MIDORI SUGIHARA
COUNSELOR OF BORDER CONTROL REFORM

31
00:02:09,651 --> 00:02:11,611
Information is split vertically,

32
00:02:11,694 --> 00:02:13,988
<i>and the front lines</i>
<i>are always one step behind.</i>

33
00:02:17,408 --> 00:02:20,245
CHIKA KUMAGAWA - GROUND STAFF

34
00:02:21,537 --> 00:02:23,122
-Yes, this way.
-Please, forward.

35
00:02:23,206 --> 00:02:24,249
Hello!

36
00:02:40,765 --> 00:02:44,686
Flight 2 has arrived.
Guiding 57 passengers now.

37
00:02:45,270 --> 00:02:49,816
To break down these vertical walls,
a special unit led by me

38
00:02:49,899 --> 00:02:51,234
that transcends the boundaries

39
00:02:51,317 --> 00:02:52,986
between ministries and agencies
will begin operation.

40
00:02:54,112 --> 00:02:54,988
<i>That operation is…</i>

41
00:03:46,914 --> 00:03:48,541
Don't say it like it's an afterthought.

42
00:04:28,664 --> 00:04:29,665
Mori? What are you doing?

43
00:04:31,084 --> 00:04:33,753
Well, this part got dirty.

44
00:04:35,838 --> 00:04:38,633
We have to take good care of our things.

45
00:04:56,984 --> 00:04:59,070
-She touched it…
-What, is that bad?

46
00:04:59,153 --> 00:05:01,447
We only handle them
during basic inspections.

47
00:05:01,531 --> 00:05:03,699
If anything happens, it leads to trouble.

48
00:05:32,353 --> 00:05:34,564
Did you do this?

49
00:05:35,231 --> 00:05:36,649
No…

50
00:05:46,117 --> 00:05:48,161
What are you going to do about it?

51
00:05:48,244 --> 00:05:52,165
Um, no, it wasn't me, uh…

52
00:05:52,248 --> 00:05:53,374
Oh, come on…

53
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:56,460
Excuse me, ma'am.
Did something happen to your luggage?

54
00:05:56,544 --> 00:05:59,797
My suitcase has been crushed.

55
00:06:01,507 --> 00:06:02,383
I'll take care of this.

56
00:06:02,466 --> 00:06:03,926
Thank you.

57
00:06:06,387 --> 00:06:08,264
-This way, please.
-Go ahead.

58
00:06:09,807 --> 00:06:11,684
-I'll take a look at your passport.
-Of course.

59
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,112
IMMIGRATION PASSPORT READING SYSTEM

60
00:06:26,866 --> 00:06:28,034
2026, MARCH 22 - QUESTIONED AT HONG KONG

61
00:06:28,117 --> 00:06:29,285
NOT DENIED ENTRY

62
00:06:30,786 --> 00:06:33,206
-What did you come to Japan for?
-Just sightseeing.

63
00:06:33,289 --> 00:06:34,665
How long will you stay for?

64
00:06:34,749 --> 00:06:36,125
About five days.

65
00:06:38,711 --> 00:06:39,754
Could you look at his luggage?

66
00:06:40,755 --> 00:06:41,672
This way.

67
00:06:42,423 --> 00:06:43,299
Huh?

68
00:06:44,091 --> 00:06:46,677
Please open that man's luggage.

69
00:06:47,803 --> 00:06:49,096
Is something suspicious about him?

70
00:06:49,972 --> 00:06:52,642
I can't share details.
It's Immigration Intelligence.

71
00:06:54,101 --> 00:06:56,687
Just open it up.
That's all I need you to do.

72
00:06:56,771 --> 00:06:59,774
No, Customs makes its own determinations.

73
00:07:00,608 --> 00:07:01,943
What are you trying to check for?

74
00:07:03,611 --> 00:07:06,906
Immigration exams people.
Customs exams items.

75
00:07:07,531 --> 00:07:08,616
Let's keep to our own domains.

76
00:07:09,283 --> 00:07:11,786
Give me a reason.
I can't open it otherwise.

77
00:07:13,663 --> 00:07:15,790
I am a professional at reading people.

78
00:07:18,125 --> 00:07:19,961
-Is that seriously your reason?
-Yes.

79
00:07:21,128 --> 00:07:22,338
What is this?

80
00:07:23,005 --> 00:07:25,550
Don't be so arrogant,
Mr. Immigration Agent.

81
00:07:25,633 --> 00:07:26,676
I am Hayami.

82
00:07:27,927 --> 00:07:30,263
Customs officers are so hard-headed.

83
00:07:31,681 --> 00:07:32,765
My name's Matsuyama!

84
00:07:37,311 --> 00:07:38,688
What's wrong?

85
00:07:38,771 --> 00:07:40,815
Chief Officer…

86
00:07:40,898 --> 00:07:42,483
Excuse me…

87
00:07:43,025 --> 00:07:46,904
-May I inspect this luggage?
-Hey, what do you think you're doing?

88
00:07:49,031 --> 00:07:49,907
Fine.

89
00:07:57,039 --> 00:07:59,250
This suitcase is heavy.

90
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:01,168
-Heavy?
-Yes.

91
00:08:01,252 --> 00:08:03,796
Especially near the bottom.

92
00:08:03,879 --> 00:08:06,215
Enough to crush the bag
that was underneath it.

93
00:08:06,299 --> 00:08:08,175
Is there something heavy inside?

94
00:08:08,843 --> 00:08:11,512
-The scale is there.
-Most likely the wheels.

95
00:08:12,888 --> 00:08:14,765
These wheels are strange.

96
00:08:15,391 --> 00:08:19,687
The wheels on all the other suitcases
were warm from the outside temperature,

97
00:08:19,770 --> 00:08:24,275
but these wheels are as cool
as the air-conditioned room.

98
00:08:24,859 --> 00:08:25,693
Meaning?

99
00:08:26,319 --> 00:08:28,529
The material of these wheels isn't rubber.

100
00:08:28,613 --> 00:08:31,824
It's a heavy metal with high thermal
conductivity and high specific gravity.

101
00:08:31,907 --> 00:08:33,242
In other words, it's basically--

102
00:08:33,326 --> 00:08:35,036
Don't touch that!

103
00:08:51,594 --> 00:08:53,304
Whoa, whoa, whoa…

104
00:09:03,773 --> 00:09:05,399
Oh my…

105
00:09:06,651 --> 00:09:09,236
BORDER CONTROL

106
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:11,906
<i>This morning</i>
<i>at Kanto International Airport,</i>

107
00:09:11,989 --> 00:09:14,450
<i>the Metropolitan Police Department</i>
<i>arrested</i>

108
00:09:14,533 --> 00:09:16,535
<i>a foreign national on suspicion</i>

109
00:09:16,619 --> 00:09:18,704
<i>of attempting to smuggle gold bullion…</i>

110
00:09:18,788 --> 00:09:21,499
Why are the police getting all the credit?

111
00:09:21,582 --> 00:09:24,877
Gate 24 wasn't mentioned even once!

112
00:09:25,503 --> 00:09:27,129
Counselor Sugihara.

113
00:09:27,213 --> 00:09:30,091
Congratulations on the launch
of the new unit.

114
00:09:30,174 --> 00:09:31,258
Airport Director Ikeura.

115
00:09:31,342 --> 00:09:32,176
TAKAHIRO IKEURA
DIRECTOR OF KANTO INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

116
00:09:32,259 --> 00:09:33,552
Breaking down the walls
between ministries and agencies.

117
00:09:33,636 --> 00:09:35,805
A truly admirable concept.

118
00:09:36,889 --> 00:09:40,810
However, as someone responsible
for running the airport,

119
00:09:41,394 --> 00:09:42,728
I have been hearing some concerns.

120
00:09:43,354 --> 00:09:44,271
Concerns?

121
00:09:44,355 --> 00:09:46,148
When there's a problem,

122
00:09:46,232 --> 00:09:49,485
who makes the decision,
and who takes the blame?

123
00:09:50,111 --> 00:09:52,822
You need to make that clear.

124
00:09:52,905 --> 00:09:55,449
Those of us on the ground

125
00:09:55,533 --> 00:09:58,494
can't operate on ideals alone, you know.

126
00:09:58,994 --> 00:09:59,995
Good day.

127
00:10:12,174 --> 00:10:14,385
It doesn't seem like
all the ministries and agencies

128
00:10:14,468 --> 00:10:17,096
are being very cooperative.

129
00:10:17,179 --> 00:10:20,808
Everyone cares more about
their own turf than the country.

130
00:10:22,727 --> 00:10:26,689
And the location is practically
a deserted island too.

131
00:10:26,772 --> 00:10:27,815
Yes.

132
00:10:29,024 --> 00:10:31,569
For now, it's a six-month trial operation,

133
00:10:32,361 --> 00:10:34,488
handling mostly temporary
and charter flights.

134
00:10:34,572 --> 00:10:37,116
<i>Basically, we're being treated</i>
<i>as benchwarmers.</i>

135
00:10:37,199 --> 00:10:38,367
<i>Benchwarmers, huh?</i>

136
00:10:38,451 --> 00:10:39,744
I suppose I am

137
00:10:40,369 --> 00:10:43,456
an old hearing officer
nearing retirement myself.

138
00:10:43,539 --> 00:10:46,000
You're Chief Hearing Officer.

139
00:10:47,710 --> 00:10:49,420
Having you on board, Fukasawa,

140
00:10:49,503 --> 00:10:51,630
gives me so much reassurance.

141
00:10:51,714 --> 00:10:52,965
I'm honored.

142
00:10:54,425 --> 00:10:55,426
Besides,

143
00:10:56,218 --> 00:10:58,763
I actually like this team.

144
00:11:00,723 --> 00:11:04,018
I heard it was a motley crew thrown
together from various departments,

145
00:11:04,101 --> 00:11:07,438
but they seem like
quite an interesting group.

146
00:11:08,606 --> 00:11:12,443
The next flight will be
the last one handled by Gate 24 today.

147
00:11:12,526 --> 00:11:14,820
Ah, I'm exhausted…

148
00:11:14,904 --> 00:11:17,948
I've been moving since the morning.
My feet have hit their limit.

149
00:11:18,032 --> 00:11:19,909
My bangs have hit their limit too.

150
00:11:21,285 --> 00:11:23,704
Everyone, just one last push.

151
00:11:25,456 --> 00:11:27,166
Matsuyama, are you listening?

152
00:11:27,249 --> 00:11:28,792
Did you see this?

153
00:11:28,876 --> 00:11:30,711
Only 500 views.

154
00:11:31,212 --> 00:11:34,840
Gate 24… It isn't
being talked about at all.

155
00:11:34,924 --> 00:11:38,802
Excuse me, customs officer, personal web
browsing during work hours isn't allowed…

156
00:11:38,886 --> 00:11:42,014
Aren't you guys in Immigration
and Quarantine frustrated too?

157
00:11:42,097 --> 00:11:44,183
After all the effort
to launch this new unit…

158
00:11:44,266 --> 00:11:45,518
But isn't the general public

159
00:11:45,601 --> 00:11:49,146
pretty uninterested in Immigration,
Customs, and Quarantine anyway?

160
00:11:49,230 --> 00:11:51,398
I feel like people
don't even know the difference.

161
00:11:52,608 --> 00:11:55,027
It is not something
we should concern ourselves with.

162
00:11:55,528 --> 00:11:58,489
Let through those who should be
and stop those who should not be.

163
00:11:58,572 --> 00:12:00,699
That is all we need to do.

164
00:12:00,783 --> 00:12:02,076
Exactly!

165
00:12:02,576 --> 00:12:05,329
That is the exact mission
entrusted to Gate 24.

166
00:12:05,412 --> 00:12:07,498
As expected of the Ministry of Justice!

167
00:12:07,581 --> 00:12:09,542
As expected of a career official!

168
00:12:12,753 --> 00:12:14,505
Is that guy a career official?

169
00:12:14,588 --> 00:12:16,882
They say he's a future candidate
for management,

170
00:12:16,966 --> 00:12:19,218
but he volunteered because he wanted
to work on the front lines,

171
00:12:19,301 --> 00:12:21,679
and he went through
proper training before coming here.

172
00:12:21,762 --> 00:12:23,222
Why go out of his way to do that?

173
00:12:23,305 --> 00:12:26,058
Because if you don't know the front lines,
you can't design system policies.

174
00:12:26,141 --> 00:12:27,810
Wonderful!

175
00:12:27,893 --> 00:12:30,563
Those words are practically
the constitution!

176
00:12:31,564 --> 00:12:34,441
Still, it's a problem
to only focus on people.

177
00:12:34,525 --> 00:12:37,570
Over here, we have to look at the goods.

178
00:12:38,279 --> 00:12:40,614
Danger isn't necessarily limited
to people, after all.

179
00:12:46,245 --> 00:12:50,791
By the way, what's she about?

180
00:12:50,874 --> 00:12:52,626
Well, I don't really know either.

181
00:12:53,294 --> 00:12:56,380
I usually hear about most things,

182
00:12:56,463 --> 00:12:58,507
but regarding that girl,
I've got zero information.

183
00:12:58,591 --> 00:13:00,634
She just keeps wiping things down.

184
00:13:01,468 --> 00:13:02,636
Mori.

185
00:13:04,305 --> 00:13:05,347
Machi Mori.

186
00:13:08,684 --> 00:13:09,518
Yes?

187
00:13:10,102 --> 00:13:12,896
Where was your previous
field assignment, Mori?

188
00:13:13,564 --> 00:13:14,732
Field assignment…

189
00:13:18,527 --> 00:13:20,321
This is my first time.

190
00:13:23,198 --> 00:13:27,411
<i>Announcement for passengers.</i>

191
00:13:27,494 --> 00:13:30,039
<i>Southeast Asia Airlines Flight 226</i>

192
00:13:30,122 --> 00:13:33,208
<i>from Ho Chi Minh City</i>
<i>will arrive at Gate 24.</i>

193
00:13:34,835 --> 00:13:37,296
We'll take our luggage. Please proceed.

194
00:13:37,379 --> 00:13:41,175
There are two booths.
Please proceed in the line.

195
00:13:47,681 --> 00:13:50,267
What does she mean this is her first time?

196
00:13:50,893 --> 00:13:53,604
I doubt she's a complete rookie, though.

197
00:13:54,730 --> 00:13:56,940
She's wiping things again…

198
00:14:05,949 --> 00:14:07,910
Passports, please.

199
00:14:17,961 --> 00:14:19,463
Please take your luggage over here.

200
00:14:21,215 --> 00:14:23,342
-Is this all your luggage?
-Yes.

201
00:14:23,425 --> 00:14:25,844
-Do you have anything to declare?
-No.

202
00:14:25,928 --> 00:14:26,804
That's all right.

203
00:14:29,056 --> 00:14:30,432
Are you traveling?

204
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:34,228
-It's our honeymoon. Honeymoon.
-Yes.

205
00:14:34,311 --> 00:14:36,605
My wife comes to Japan a lot.
She loves it here, so…

206
00:14:37,648 --> 00:14:38,524
I can see that.

207
00:14:50,285 --> 00:14:51,829
How long do you plan to stay?

208
00:14:52,329 --> 00:14:53,455
Two weeks.

209
00:14:59,795 --> 00:15:01,588
Please step this way and use this booth.

210
00:15:02,589 --> 00:15:04,800
Could I have a moment with both of you?

211
00:15:08,929 --> 00:15:10,681
-Please take their luggage.
-Okay.

212
00:15:11,223 --> 00:15:12,057
This way.

213
00:15:21,692 --> 00:15:23,485
Please, have a seat.

214
00:15:24,653 --> 00:15:27,072
Why… Why did you bring us here?

215
00:15:27,156 --> 00:15:28,949
It's just a formal check.

216
00:15:32,786 --> 00:15:35,289
Excuse me. What do I do with this luggage?

217
00:15:35,372 --> 00:15:36,623
Keep it with the passengers.

218
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:39,710
Please wait here a moment.

219
00:15:48,135 --> 00:15:49,803
Did something happen again?

220
00:15:51,388 --> 00:15:52,598
Hayami!

221
00:15:52,681 --> 00:15:55,642
-Seike, what about the inspections?
-I had Natori take over for me?

222
00:15:57,269 --> 00:15:59,146
Um…

223
00:16:00,355 --> 00:16:02,149
I saw you do this earlier.

224
00:16:04,359 --> 00:16:05,444
What is that?

225
00:16:07,154 --> 00:16:09,615
That's a hand signal
we've established in Immigration.

226
00:16:09,698 --> 00:16:10,824
It's a signal for a suspicious person.

227
00:16:10,908 --> 00:16:13,410
I see. A hand signal…

228
00:16:16,997 --> 00:16:19,124
So those two really are suspicious, right?

229
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,878
-Just tell me already.
-I said, this is Immigration Intelligence.

230
00:16:22,961 --> 00:16:24,880
Excuse me…

231
00:16:26,256 --> 00:16:28,592
<i>To break down these vertical walls,</i>

232
00:16:28,675 --> 00:16:30,969
-What are you doing?
-<i>starting today, a special unit led by me</i>

233
00:16:31,053 --> 00:16:32,429
that transcends the boundaries

234
00:16:32,513 --> 00:16:34,723
between ministries and agencies
will begin operation.

235
00:16:35,224 --> 00:16:37,518
That is what she said.

236
00:16:37,601 --> 00:16:42,272
So, in other words, at Gate 24,
we share information,

237
00:16:42,356 --> 00:16:43,190
right?

238
00:16:44,066 --> 00:16:45,359
That's…

239
00:16:45,901 --> 00:16:49,696
Yes. I was so happy about the whole thing,
I rewatched it many times.

240
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:52,825
These are the words
of Counselor Midori Sugihara

241
00:16:52,908 --> 00:16:55,077
from the Cabinet Secretariat
Border Control Reform Office.

242
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:56,453
<i>Gate 24</i>

243
00:16:57,287 --> 00:16:59,206
<i>is a brand new system, so…</i>

244
00:16:59,289 --> 00:17:01,458
Indeed… Hayami.

245
00:17:01,542 --> 00:17:04,253
-We should work as a team and share--
-Provided that

246
00:17:05,254 --> 00:17:06,421
nothing leaks to the outside.

247
00:17:07,673 --> 00:17:08,799
Of course.

248
00:17:10,217 --> 00:17:11,593
You too.

249
00:17:11,677 --> 00:17:15,013
Yes. Information is shared.
Confidentiality is strict.

250
00:17:19,935 --> 00:17:22,813
Regarding that couple,
the husband is Samir Sadikov.

251
00:17:22,896 --> 00:17:24,064
The wife is Lylea Sadikova.

252
00:17:24,731 --> 00:17:26,775
Both are from the Zafaria Federation.

253
00:17:27,734 --> 00:17:30,070
Before coming to Japan,
they stopped in Vietnam,

254
00:17:30,154 --> 00:17:32,865
but they were refused entry
during local inspections.

255
00:17:32,948 --> 00:17:34,158
I see.

256
00:17:35,242 --> 00:17:39,580
The Counselor is here right now as well.
Let's listen to this together.

257
00:17:41,498 --> 00:17:42,499
Excuse me.

258
00:17:46,253 --> 00:17:49,256
Did you run an inquiry on that couple?

259
00:17:49,339 --> 00:17:50,799
Yes, however,

260
00:17:50,883 --> 00:17:52,676
the current situation
in Zafaria is unstable,

261
00:17:52,759 --> 00:17:54,845
so we cannot make inquiries
with their local authorities,

262
00:17:54,928 --> 00:17:57,097
and we haven't been able
to verify their identities yet.

263
00:17:57,181 --> 00:17:58,098
I see.

264
00:17:58,182 --> 00:17:59,892
Until things are clear,

265
00:17:59,975 --> 00:18:03,937
we should consider having them wait
without permitting entry.

266
00:18:04,021 --> 00:18:06,273
-<i>Yes, sir.</i>
-Hayami.

267
00:18:06,356 --> 00:18:08,692
I'll leave the questioning
of those two to you.

268
00:18:10,903 --> 00:18:13,071
-Understood.
<i>-This is perfect.</i>

269
00:18:13,155 --> 00:18:16,992
Why not have Customs lend a hand as well?

270
00:18:17,659 --> 00:18:19,494
Counselor Sugihara…

271
00:18:19,578 --> 00:18:21,580
Customs as well?

272
00:18:21,663 --> 00:18:23,790
<i>There are things that can be seen</i>
<i>through the goods, aren't there?</i>

273
00:18:25,334 --> 00:18:26,877
Shall we give it a try?

274
00:18:28,462 --> 00:18:29,296
<i>This might be</i>

275
00:18:29,379 --> 00:18:33,383
an excellent opportunity
to demonstrate the value of Gate 24.

276
00:18:34,301 --> 00:18:36,428
I want Immigration and Customs
to work together to find the answer

277
00:18:36,511 --> 00:18:39,640
as to whether those two
should be allowed entry or not.

278
00:18:39,723 --> 00:18:41,934
Yes, leave it to us.

279
00:18:51,318 --> 00:18:52,402
Apologies for keeping you waiting.

280
00:18:53,153 --> 00:18:55,739
What's going on? Can we go?

281
00:18:55,822 --> 00:18:58,450
To help with that,
please let us ask a few questions.

282
00:19:01,078 --> 00:19:05,874
Before coming to Japan,
you two were refused entry in Vietnam.

283
00:19:06,750 --> 00:19:08,293
We don't know.

284
00:19:08,877 --> 00:19:09,795
You don't know?

285
00:19:10,879 --> 00:19:13,924
Because they didn't tell us.

286
00:19:14,007 --> 00:19:15,050
I see.

287
00:19:17,094 --> 00:19:20,138
May we check the contents of this luggage?

288
00:19:20,764 --> 00:19:22,557
Here? You go through luggage here?

289
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:26,270
Of course, it's voluntary,
but if you cooperate,

290
00:19:26,353 --> 00:19:27,354
the check will be finished quickly.

291
00:19:29,523 --> 00:19:31,316
Okay, okay. I open.

292
00:19:47,457 --> 00:19:49,710
-Are you okay?
-Get the first aid kit.

293
00:19:49,793 --> 00:19:51,128
It's okay. It's fine. It's okay.

294
00:19:51,211 --> 00:19:52,796
Just, please, check.

295
00:19:53,422 --> 00:19:54,548
Thank you.

296
00:19:55,173 --> 00:19:56,800
To ensure there are no mix-ups
upon return,

297
00:19:56,883 --> 00:19:58,969
we will record
the condition of the contents.

298
00:20:00,137 --> 00:20:01,096
I'll do it.

299
00:20:03,849 --> 00:20:04,975
Okay then.

300
00:20:05,851 --> 00:20:06,893
-Please do so.
-Yes.

301
00:20:18,238 --> 00:20:20,699
So the couple shares one piece of luggage…

302
00:20:21,241 --> 00:20:22,743
May I ask?

303
00:20:24,286 --> 00:20:28,623
You two are newlyweds,
but when and where did you meet?

304
00:20:29,207 --> 00:20:30,792
It was about, uh,

305
00:20:31,543 --> 00:20:34,087
about five years ago. Through a friend.

306
00:20:34,629 --> 00:20:35,922
I'm asking Lylea.

307
00:20:38,091 --> 00:20:39,092
Wait, hold on…

308
00:20:39,593 --> 00:20:42,679
Ah, this, yes, this. This is ours.

309
00:20:42,763 --> 00:20:43,764
I'll show…

310
00:20:44,973 --> 00:20:47,017
This is Lylea's family.

311
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:48,393
Lylea's family.

312
00:20:49,186 --> 00:20:51,605
-Show.
-Oh, yes, um…

313
00:20:52,105 --> 00:20:54,524
This… This is my older brother,

314
00:20:55,650 --> 00:20:59,404
my parents, and my little sister.

315
00:20:59,488 --> 00:21:03,200
My older brother introduced us.

316
00:21:03,950 --> 00:21:04,785
Thank you.

317
00:21:04,868 --> 00:21:07,162
They look like a close-knit family.

318
00:21:07,245 --> 00:21:09,873
That was from the party
we threw at our place.

319
00:21:25,972 --> 00:21:27,057
Is it a pair of dolls?

320
00:21:27,641 --> 00:21:28,642
Very cute.

321
00:21:29,893 --> 00:21:31,061
Yes.

322
00:21:31,144 --> 00:21:32,646
They were a wedding gift.

323
00:21:32,729 --> 00:21:36,233
Could we please just get this over with?

324
00:21:36,942 --> 00:21:38,735
We have a hotel reservation, so…

325
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:42,030
Then, continuing with the questions…

326
00:21:42,656 --> 00:21:43,615
Hayami.

327
00:21:49,413 --> 00:21:52,374
I'm Iuchi from the Metropolitan Police
Department's International Crime Division.

328
00:21:52,457 --> 00:21:54,167
-Tamai.
-Hello.

329
00:21:54,251 --> 00:21:56,545
-Someone's here.
-We were called here.

330
00:21:56,628 --> 00:21:58,088
Likewise, I'm Nakatsuka.

331
00:21:58,171 --> 00:21:59,172
Hello.

332
00:21:59,256 --> 00:22:01,883
You came because of those two.
Do you know something?

333
00:22:02,759 --> 00:22:04,261
I'll cut straight to the conclusion.

334
00:22:05,804 --> 00:22:08,932
Let those two enter.

335
00:22:10,976 --> 00:22:12,769
Why? Are those two--

336
00:22:12,853 --> 00:22:14,020
We can't share details.

337
00:22:14,104 --> 00:22:15,272
It's police intelligence.

338
00:22:17,941 --> 00:22:19,359
Are you familiar
with the Immigration Control Act?

339
00:22:20,819 --> 00:22:23,029
This decision is the duty of Immigration.

340
00:22:23,864 --> 00:22:26,992
You can't suddenly ask us to grant entry
without a formal request.

341
00:22:28,326 --> 00:22:30,537
Shut up. It's always
every little thing with you guys.

342
00:22:32,164 --> 00:22:34,916
This matter involves
a criminal investigation.

343
00:22:35,500 --> 00:22:36,668
End of story.

344
00:22:37,544 --> 00:22:41,089
You guys just need
to open and close the doors.

345
00:22:51,391 --> 00:22:52,976
Wait. What do you mean?

346
00:22:53,059 --> 00:22:55,187
They were refused entry in Vietnam,

347
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:57,063
but the Japanese police
are telling us to let them in?

348
00:22:57,147 --> 00:22:59,441
They wouldn't tell us
the reason or anything.

349
00:23:00,525 --> 00:23:02,235
Why don't we just let them in?

350
00:23:03,737 --> 00:23:05,614
Setting aside the detective's attitude,

351
00:23:05,697 --> 00:23:08,575
it means the police
will take responsibility.

352
00:23:09,326 --> 00:23:11,244
As Immigration, don't we
just have to comply?

353
00:23:11,328 --> 00:23:13,538
You're right! Shall we do that then?

354
00:23:13,622 --> 00:23:15,040
Um…

355
00:23:15,123 --> 00:23:16,833
If you talk about responsibility,

356
00:23:16,917 --> 00:23:18,627
there's also the responsibility
of letting them in.

357
00:23:19,377 --> 00:23:20,420
Well, when you put it that way…

358
00:23:20,503 --> 00:23:21,796
Um…

359
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:25,508
At present, the grounds for refusing entry
to those two are weak.

360
00:23:26,760 --> 00:23:29,179
-I suppose so.
-That doesn't mean you can just…

361
00:23:29,262 --> 00:23:30,096
Excuse me!

362
00:23:30,931 --> 00:23:32,015
Um…

363
00:23:32,098 --> 00:23:33,600
Wait, wait, Mori.

364
00:23:33,683 --> 00:23:34,684
What are you doing?

365
00:23:35,810 --> 00:23:37,812
Making my own kind of hand signal.

366
00:23:38,438 --> 00:23:41,608
-Excuse me?
-I'm glad you noticed.

367
00:23:41,691 --> 00:23:42,651
That was a signal just now?

368
00:23:42,734 --> 00:23:44,527
Yes. Um…

369
00:23:46,154 --> 00:23:48,865
-Regarding these dolls…
-Dolls?

370
00:23:48,949 --> 00:23:50,033
What are you talking about?

371
00:23:50,116 --> 00:23:53,036
Ah, the ones Lylea said
were a wedding gift.

372
00:23:53,119 --> 00:23:54,162
Yes.

373
00:23:54,246 --> 00:23:57,457
The shape of these arms
forms a semaphore signal.

374
00:23:57,540 --> 00:23:59,167
Semaphore signal?

375
00:23:59,251 --> 00:24:00,961
It's like flag signaling.

376
00:24:01,044 --> 00:24:03,421
It conveys letters of the alphabet
through arm angles.

377
00:24:04,089 --> 00:24:06,967
This shape is "E". And

378
00:24:07,550 --> 00:24:09,719
this one is "M".

379
00:24:10,345 --> 00:24:11,304
E, M?

380
00:24:11,388 --> 00:24:12,764
Emergency?

381
00:24:12,847 --> 00:24:15,308
Yes. It means an emergency situation.

382
00:24:15,392 --> 00:24:17,811
Wait a minute.
These dolls are saying that?

383
00:24:17,894 --> 00:24:21,731
Or rather, did someone move
these dolls' arms to convey that?

384
00:24:22,274 --> 00:24:23,858
I don't know.

385
00:24:23,942 --> 00:24:27,320
However, I thought this might
also be some kind of sign.

386
00:24:27,404 --> 00:24:29,864
Is that woman asking for help?

387
00:24:29,948 --> 00:24:32,742
Well, it might just be a coincidence
that they're in this shape.

388
00:24:32,826 --> 00:24:34,744
Mori, how do you even know
about these signals?

389
00:24:34,828 --> 00:24:36,246
May I investigate this in more detail?

390
00:24:36,329 --> 00:24:38,039
What, Mori?

391
00:24:42,544 --> 00:24:45,088
I want to investigate a bit more too.

392
00:24:46,089 --> 00:24:49,884
To me, it looked like Lylea was terrified.

393
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:51,594
What about you, Hayami?

394
00:24:52,387 --> 00:24:53,847
Aren't you a pro at seeing through people?

395
00:24:55,307 --> 00:24:56,808
What if she really

396
00:24:57,392 --> 00:24:59,352
is asking for help?

397
00:25:05,233 --> 00:25:06,943
Even if we investigate…

398
00:25:10,947 --> 00:25:12,073
wouldn't it just be a waste of time?

399
00:25:12,157 --> 00:25:15,952
It doesn't matter if it's a waste, right?

400
00:25:17,454 --> 00:25:21,041
That's our job, isn't it?

401
00:25:31,593 --> 00:25:35,722
Are you done yet? Huh?
Are you done yet? Yes, no?

402
00:25:35,805 --> 00:25:38,558
May we inspect your luggage one more time?

403
00:25:39,392 --> 00:25:41,895
Fine. Whatever. Fine. Okay, okay.

404
00:25:42,479 --> 00:25:44,606
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

405
00:26:11,383 --> 00:26:13,676
ANALYZING

406
00:26:17,514 --> 00:26:18,681
This is called TDS--

407
00:26:18,765 --> 00:26:21,017
It's a machine that wipes
the luggage surface

408
00:26:21,101 --> 00:26:23,186
to check for traces of drugs
or explosives.

409
00:26:25,605 --> 00:26:26,523
Right?

410
00:26:29,234 --> 00:26:30,610
Did you come to help out?

411
00:26:30,693 --> 00:26:32,529
No, this is a customs officer's work.

412
00:26:32,612 --> 00:26:33,530
Did anything come up?

413
00:26:33,613 --> 00:26:35,115
NOTHING FOUND

414
00:26:35,198 --> 00:26:37,951
No traces of illegal substances
were detected.

415
00:26:38,034 --> 00:26:39,327
A swing and a miss, then.

416
00:26:39,411 --> 00:26:41,538
If you're just here to mock us,
could you leave?

417
00:26:43,164 --> 00:26:45,166
Um…

418
00:26:48,670 --> 00:26:50,922
Regarding these keys…

419
00:26:52,882 --> 00:26:55,385
Each one of them has their own keys?

420
00:26:56,136 --> 00:26:57,011
What could these keys be for?

421
00:26:57,804 --> 00:26:59,889
This one is for a car, maybe.

422
00:26:59,973 --> 00:27:03,393
The other is a motorcycle and… a padlock?

423
00:27:04,602 --> 00:27:06,187
Then, what about this one?

424
00:27:07,772 --> 00:27:09,774
A front door key? For the couple's home.

425
00:27:10,358 --> 00:27:11,901
I think so too.

426
00:27:12,485 --> 00:27:14,195
But it's strange.

427
00:27:14,279 --> 00:27:17,323
That couple seems to be living
in the same home.

428
00:27:17,407 --> 00:27:20,034
In that case, shouldn't each spouse

429
00:27:20,118 --> 00:27:23,371
have one front door key?

430
00:27:26,499 --> 00:27:27,417
Indeed…

431
00:27:30,462 --> 00:27:33,006
It means only one of them
has the key to the house.

432
00:27:33,089 --> 00:27:36,009
-Is that normal?
-No, it's strange.

433
00:27:37,802 --> 00:27:40,263
Are those two really a married couple?

434
00:27:41,514 --> 00:27:42,932
Hey, Hayami,

435
00:27:43,641 --> 00:27:46,436
since when do you do Customs work?

436
00:27:48,521 --> 00:27:49,397
Excuse me.

437
00:27:54,861 --> 00:27:56,946
I'm also curious about this key.

438
00:27:57,030 --> 00:27:58,531
What key could it be?

439
00:27:58,615 --> 00:28:01,493
A key to a warehouse
somewhere or something?

440
00:28:02,327 --> 00:28:06,581
You notice a lot of things, don't you,
Mori? Your knowledge is broad too.

441
00:28:07,332 --> 00:28:08,708
What were you doing up until now?

442
00:28:14,214 --> 00:28:15,590
Are you listening?

443
00:28:15,673 --> 00:28:17,634
Oh, are you in the middle of something?

444
00:28:17,717 --> 00:28:20,386
We looked into that couple.

445
00:28:22,096 --> 00:28:25,683
Tamai reached out to all her connections
across the airport.

446
00:28:25,767 --> 00:28:28,770
We were able to hear from staff
knowledgeable about international crime.

447
00:28:28,853 --> 00:28:30,313
You have acquaintances like that?

448
00:28:30,396 --> 00:28:33,650
I live purely on human connections.

449
00:28:33,733 --> 00:28:36,528
Endo also looked into local news articles.

450
00:28:36,611 --> 00:28:38,947
For Quarantine, information
is life, after all. Low-key.

451
00:28:39,030 --> 00:28:40,865
And from that,
we found out that right now,

452
00:28:40,949 --> 00:28:43,785
a human trafficking group from Zafaria

453
00:28:43,868 --> 00:28:45,787
is active across all of Asia.

454
00:28:45,870 --> 00:28:47,288
That organization

455
00:28:47,372 --> 00:28:49,707
doesn't just target the individual,
but their entire family as well, it seems.

456
00:28:50,416 --> 00:28:52,502
-The entire family?
-Then,

457
00:28:53,044 --> 00:28:54,629
those two…

458
00:28:55,672 --> 00:28:57,298
Samir

459
00:28:57,382 --> 00:28:59,092
is a broker for the organization,

460
00:28:59,175 --> 00:29:00,677
and Lylea's family was taken hostage,

461
00:29:00,760 --> 00:29:02,720
and she was brought to Japan
against her will,

462
00:29:02,804 --> 00:29:04,472
or so I presume.

463
00:29:04,556 --> 00:29:05,932
Seriously?

464
00:29:08,309 --> 00:29:11,271
But that makes everything add up.

465
00:29:11,354 --> 00:29:15,900
They're a fake couple,
which is why there was only one house key.

466
00:29:15,984 --> 00:29:18,820
Plus, Lylea has been
to Japan multiple times,

467
00:29:18,903 --> 00:29:21,614
so she's highly valuable to Samir.

468
00:29:21,698 --> 00:29:22,824
For getting through
immigration inspection too.

469
00:29:22,907 --> 00:29:24,325
-That's true.
-Hey.

470
00:29:25,410 --> 00:29:28,204
-What do you think?
-What are you going to do?

471
00:29:30,957 --> 00:29:32,959
You're not being very clear.

472
00:29:34,502 --> 00:29:37,839
In the end, Hayami, you just don't
want to take responsibility, right?

473
00:29:40,174 --> 00:29:42,594
Now, now, it's still speculation.

474
00:29:42,677 --> 00:29:44,804
For now, let's report to Fukasawa.

475
00:29:48,349 --> 00:29:51,644
You haven't let them into the country yet?

476
00:29:59,193 --> 00:30:01,154
Well, yes, the police

477
00:30:01,237 --> 00:30:06,284
had also caught onto the possibility
that Samir was connected

478
00:30:06,367 --> 00:30:07,827
to a human trafficking ring.

479
00:30:09,120 --> 00:30:11,706
You wanted to let him enter
rather than arrest him here,

480
00:30:11,789 --> 00:30:13,082
to get the tail of the organization.

481
00:30:13,166 --> 00:30:14,167
Was that the goal?

482
00:30:14,250 --> 00:30:16,628
So that's what's going on…

483
00:30:16,711 --> 00:30:20,089
-But we can't at least protect Lylea?
-Doing something like that

484
00:30:20,173 --> 00:30:23,593
would be as good as notifying
the target that the police suspect them.

485
00:30:23,676 --> 00:30:25,762
Well, that's true…

486
00:30:25,845 --> 00:30:27,180
Hey, what even is this place?

487
00:30:28,264 --> 00:30:31,434
Are you sharing Immigration Intelligence
with Customs and Quarantine here?

488
00:30:31,517 --> 00:30:34,395
-Well, that's…
-Yes.

489
00:30:34,479 --> 00:30:35,813
A special unit that transcends
the boundaries

490
00:30:35,897 --> 00:30:36,940
between ministries and agencies.

491
00:30:37,023 --> 00:30:39,567
This is Gate 24.

492
00:30:42,445 --> 00:30:43,363
Right?

493
00:30:45,657 --> 00:30:47,909
-Something like that's impossible.
-Right?

494
00:30:48,618 --> 00:30:51,579
At any rate, hurry up the procedures.

495
00:30:51,663 --> 00:30:55,541
If the target catches wind
of the police presence, it's all over.

496
00:30:55,625 --> 00:30:58,252
Can you take responsibility
if that happens?

497
00:31:03,383 --> 00:31:04,509
-Understood.
-Alright.

498
00:31:04,592 --> 00:31:05,551
Hey, Hayami…

499
00:31:05,635 --> 00:31:07,929
-It's a police request.
-Even so,

500
00:31:08,012 --> 00:31:09,722
Are you just going
to leave Lylea with him?

501
00:31:11,140 --> 00:31:13,226
Even though she sent a help signal?

502
00:31:14,352 --> 00:31:17,146
Is Immigration fine with that?

503
00:31:20,692 --> 00:31:21,985
It's not my call.

504
00:31:27,991 --> 00:31:29,867
Don't say it so lightly.

505
00:31:31,077 --> 00:31:33,788
Customs can't even take responsibility,
so you should stay out of this.

506
00:31:38,501 --> 00:31:40,545
Well, now, thank you, everyone,
for your hard work.

507
00:31:40,628 --> 00:31:41,671
Fukusawa…

508
00:31:42,380 --> 00:31:46,050
-I am Chief Hearing Officer Fukasawa.
-Oh, hello.

509
00:31:46,134 --> 00:31:47,677
I have heard the circumstances.

510
00:31:48,428 --> 00:31:52,181
The final decision regarding entry
will be made by me.

511
00:31:52,265 --> 00:31:55,184
Then give the go-ahead now.

512
00:31:55,852 --> 00:31:57,520
Don't be in such a rush.

513
00:31:57,603 --> 00:32:01,149
Actually, officials
from the Ministry of Justice

514
00:32:01,232 --> 00:32:05,903
and National Police Agency
are currently conferring on this matter.

515
00:32:06,529 --> 00:32:07,947
Let's wait for their conclusion,

516
00:32:10,491 --> 00:32:13,786
or would acting on your own in the field

517
00:32:14,287 --> 00:32:17,290
turn into a responsibility issue itself?

518
00:32:43,399 --> 00:32:44,650
What are you doing?

519
00:32:45,318 --> 00:32:46,402
Investigating.

520
00:32:47,070 --> 00:32:48,279
That's enough.

521
00:32:48,780 --> 00:32:50,490
There's nothing more
the front line can do.

522
00:32:56,162 --> 00:32:58,081
It's just as the police said.

523
00:32:59,457 --> 00:33:01,542
A unit like this was impossible.

524
00:33:02,794 --> 00:33:05,254
Immigration and Customs
are completely different.

525
00:33:06,547 --> 00:33:08,966
Customs looks at goods. If there's
something illegal, they stop it.

526
00:33:09,050 --> 00:33:10,802
If not, they let it pass.

527
00:33:10,885 --> 00:33:12,720
It's black and white.

528
00:33:14,180 --> 00:33:16,349
But Immigration deals with people.

529
00:33:16,432 --> 00:33:19,060
More often than not,
it can't be divided into black or white.

530
00:33:19,811 --> 00:33:22,897
So while it remains gray,
a line has to be drawn somewhere.

531
00:33:26,025 --> 00:33:28,236
You should just call it quits too now.

532
00:33:28,778 --> 00:33:30,613
Because this matter
is already covered in gray.

533
00:33:30,696 --> 00:33:32,073
Um…

534
00:33:36,369 --> 00:33:39,247
What color is that gray?

535
00:33:40,540 --> 00:33:42,708
-Excuse me?
-Even if you say it's gray,

536
00:33:42,792 --> 00:33:44,627
there are many kinds.

537
00:33:44,710 --> 00:33:47,130
Gray close to white, gray close to black.

538
00:33:47,839 --> 00:33:50,383
Gray mixed with blue or red.

539
00:33:50,466 --> 00:33:52,426
There are countless types.

540
00:33:53,970 --> 00:33:57,598
What color gray is this matter?

541
00:34:03,020 --> 00:34:05,857
I want to know that.

542
00:34:06,607 --> 00:34:12,029
Because I dislike leaving things
I don't understand unknown.

543
00:34:22,081 --> 00:34:23,332
This zipper…

544
00:34:25,501 --> 00:34:30,047
Look, this zipper is made
of flexible resin and is easy to close.

545
00:34:32,508 --> 00:34:33,551
What about it?

546
00:34:38,097 --> 00:34:39,182
What are you doing there?

547
00:34:40,141 --> 00:34:41,475
Counselor Sugihara…

548
00:34:43,728 --> 00:34:45,188
A conclusion has been reached.

549
00:34:45,813 --> 00:34:47,982
They say to grant entry to the two.

550
00:34:48,065 --> 00:34:51,569
So we're just going
to leave Lylea with him…

551
00:34:52,236 --> 00:34:55,489
I'm worried, but I suppose
it can't be helped.

552
00:34:56,365 --> 00:34:57,783
Well then, Hayami,

553
00:34:58,326 --> 00:35:00,453
could I ask you to handle
their entry procedures?

554
00:35:02,955 --> 00:35:04,582
Are you unhappy with something?

555
00:35:05,666 --> 00:35:08,127
No, it's a decision from above.

556
00:35:09,670 --> 00:35:10,504
It's just

557
00:35:11,005 --> 00:35:12,423
this one thing.

558
00:35:19,347 --> 00:35:22,350
I've been bothered
by this photo the whole time.

559
00:35:22,934 --> 00:35:24,518
Everyone in the family is smiling,

560
00:35:25,269 --> 00:35:27,688
but somehow, they look tense.

561
00:35:27,772 --> 00:35:28,940
Tense?

562
00:35:31,234 --> 00:35:32,526
For instance…

563
00:35:33,152 --> 00:35:36,113
-Okay, say cheese!
-<i>What if when this photo was taken,</i>

564
00:35:36,197 --> 00:35:37,782
-Okay!
-<i>Lylea</i>

565
00:35:37,865 --> 00:35:40,910
<i>and her entire family</i>
<i>had already been abducted</i>

566
00:35:40,993 --> 00:35:45,164
<i>and a gun was being pointed</i>
<i>at them from behind the camera?</i>

567
00:35:46,290 --> 00:35:48,167
Even if we let those two pass like this,

568
00:35:48,834 --> 00:35:51,254
I wonder if Lylea's family
will really be okay?

569
00:35:53,089 --> 00:35:56,634
That said, it's just speculation.
Besides, it's too late now.

570
00:35:57,260 --> 00:35:58,302
No,

571
00:35:58,844 --> 00:36:00,554
it's worth investigating.

572
00:36:01,973 --> 00:36:05,601
Shall I negotiate with the top
to buy us just a little more time?

573
00:36:06,269 --> 00:36:07,812
In the meantime,

574
00:36:08,562 --> 00:36:10,022
whether it's a clue about the organization

575
00:36:10,898 --> 00:36:13,609
or Lylea's family, anything goes.

576
00:36:13,693 --> 00:36:16,279
Find grounds enough to stop those two.

577
00:36:16,362 --> 00:36:19,031
-No, but, like I said, this was just--
-Let's do it.

578
00:36:19,699 --> 00:36:21,367
If it comes down to responsibility,
I will take it.

579
00:36:22,910 --> 00:36:24,412
Incredible…

580
00:36:24,495 --> 00:36:27,707
-So cool…
-All right, let's go, go, go.

581
00:36:34,463 --> 00:36:36,549
Apologies for keeping you waiting.

582
00:36:36,632 --> 00:36:38,718
-I am Chief Hearing Officer Fukasawa.
-What now?

583
00:36:38,801 --> 00:36:41,554
How long do you plan
on keeping us for? Huh?

584
00:36:41,637 --> 00:36:42,763
I am very sorry.

585
00:36:43,431 --> 00:36:46,934
Last step. Please allow us to speak
with each of you individually.

586
00:36:48,019 --> 00:36:50,187
One by one, huh? One by one?

587
00:36:50,271 --> 00:36:52,440
Starting with yourself.

588
00:36:54,317 --> 00:36:56,652
I refuse. No. No!

589
00:36:56,736 --> 00:37:01,324
If you comply,
we won't detain you any longer.

590
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:06,037
Okay, but this is it.
After, you'll let us go.

591
00:37:07,621 --> 00:37:08,789
This way, please.

592
00:37:23,596 --> 00:37:25,806
What's going on? What?

593
00:37:25,890 --> 00:37:28,017
He won't be back for a while.

594
00:37:28,559 --> 00:37:31,062
Could you tell me in detail
about the situation

595
00:37:31,979 --> 00:37:33,481
you are currently in?

596
00:37:40,196 --> 00:37:44,492
I see. So they split the two up.

597
00:37:45,326 --> 00:37:49,413
-I hope it goes well.
-It comes down to Hayami, then…

598
00:37:50,247 --> 00:37:53,793
We got some time. But only 30 minutes.

599
00:37:53,876 --> 00:37:55,044
That's short…

600
00:38:00,383 --> 00:38:01,300
Lylea.

601
00:38:02,468 --> 00:38:05,096
We got the message in your luggage.

602
00:38:05,846 --> 00:38:08,224
We also have a lead on that man

603
00:38:08,891 --> 00:38:10,476
and that your family

604
00:38:11,102 --> 00:38:13,396
is currently in a dangerous situation.

605
00:38:15,147 --> 00:38:17,566
All we need now is to hear it from you.

606
00:38:20,111 --> 00:38:21,612
Please, speak to us.

607
00:38:26,534 --> 00:38:28,536
Look, there's no time.
Let's search for evidence over here too.

608
00:38:28,619 --> 00:38:29,745
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

609
00:38:30,371 --> 00:38:32,248
You tell us to look for evidence, but…

610
00:38:32,957 --> 00:38:35,000
Don't the police have any information?

611
00:38:35,084 --> 00:38:36,794
Like the identity of the organization.

612
00:38:37,336 --> 00:38:39,380
We don't know their exact base,

613
00:38:39,463 --> 00:38:42,174
but we've narrowed it down to some extent.

614
00:38:42,258 --> 00:38:43,551
Whereabouts?

615
00:38:43,634 --> 00:38:45,428
-We can't tell you that.
-That's right.

616
00:38:45,511 --> 00:38:47,430
Um…

617
00:38:47,972 --> 00:38:50,391
Is that base in Aichi Prefecture?

618
00:38:50,474 --> 00:38:51,600
That's right. What?!

619
00:38:53,352 --> 00:38:56,147
This photo is strange.

620
00:38:57,982 --> 00:39:01,360
-This tree looks like a Hananoki.
-Hananoki?

621
00:39:01,444 --> 00:39:03,237
It's a tree unique to Japan.

622
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:06,323
It's distributed mainly in limited areas
of the Chubu region

623
00:39:06,407 --> 00:39:08,659
and is also the prefectural tree
of Aichi Prefecture.

624
00:39:08,742 --> 00:39:10,578
It shouldn't be seen in Zafaria.

625
00:39:10,661 --> 00:39:12,121
What? Then, this photo was…

626
00:39:12,204 --> 00:39:13,873
Taken in Japan?

627
00:39:13,956 --> 00:39:15,708
Excuse me a second here.

628
00:39:16,250 --> 00:39:17,460
Then what about this utility pole?

629
00:39:17,543 --> 00:39:20,045
Doesn't it provide some clue?

630
00:39:20,713 --> 00:39:22,298
I don't see anything.

631
00:39:22,381 --> 00:39:24,508
I don't know if it will, but…

632
00:39:27,887 --> 00:39:31,140
Utility poles have plates with
identification numbers written on them,

633
00:39:31,223 --> 00:39:33,726
which serve as the address
of the utility pole.

634
00:39:33,809 --> 00:39:35,853
That's a huge clue.

635
00:39:35,936 --> 00:39:39,273
Lylea, please, tell us the truth.

636
00:39:40,191 --> 00:39:43,486
We will protect you and your family
with all our strength.

637
00:39:43,569 --> 00:39:47,072
Please, trust us.

638
00:39:52,286 --> 00:39:54,622
Are you really going to protect me?

639
00:39:56,832 --> 00:39:58,083
Of course.

640
00:40:01,462 --> 00:40:02,755
That man…

641
00:40:04,632 --> 00:40:06,050
is not my husband.

642
00:40:07,885 --> 00:40:09,512
The truth is…

643
00:40:34,161 --> 00:40:36,622
Okay. Let us through.

644
00:40:44,547 --> 00:40:45,798
Wait.

645
00:40:46,465 --> 00:40:48,300
We apologize,

646
00:40:48,384 --> 00:40:50,219
but entry cannot be permitted.

647
00:40:50,302 --> 00:40:55,516
You are suspected of being involved
with a human trafficking organization.

648
00:40:56,892 --> 00:40:58,602
What the hell are you talking about? No.

649
00:40:59,395 --> 00:41:01,564
Fukusawa, what's going on?

650
00:41:01,647 --> 00:41:05,025
We located the place
where your family was being confined.

651
00:41:23,752 --> 00:41:27,214
It's okay, it's okay, it's okay.

652
00:41:31,802 --> 00:41:34,346
-Entire family found.
-Clear!

653
00:41:34,888 --> 00:41:36,056
Don't move!

654
00:41:38,767 --> 00:41:40,102
Don't move!

655
00:41:41,687 --> 00:41:43,897
-What now?
-Hey!

656
00:41:43,981 --> 00:41:45,149
What was that?

657
00:41:46,567 --> 00:41:49,612
It wasn't me. It was not me.

658
00:41:49,695 --> 00:41:52,281
-Bring him up.
-Stand up.

659
00:41:52,990 --> 00:41:57,494
Hideout suppressed. Family secured.

660
00:41:58,329 --> 00:41:59,371
Also…

661
00:42:01,040 --> 00:42:02,625
from the criminal group at the hideout,

662
00:42:02,708 --> 00:42:05,753
we obtained information on the broker,
who was the mastermind.

663
00:42:14,345 --> 00:42:17,514
Lylea Sadikova. Or rather,
real name, Nadia Karimova.

664
00:42:25,230 --> 00:42:27,566
-Don't move!
-Stop!

665
00:42:27,650 --> 00:42:30,069
-Stop!
-Don't touch me!

666
00:42:30,152 --> 00:42:32,112
Stop resisting!

667
00:42:32,988 --> 00:42:34,156
We're borrowing a room.

668
00:42:35,240 --> 00:42:36,742
Let me go!

669
00:42:44,124 --> 00:42:45,834
My family? Are they safe?

670
00:42:45,918 --> 00:42:46,877
Yes.

671
00:42:47,544 --> 00:42:48,921
It's okay now.

672
00:42:49,004 --> 00:42:51,965
H-how?

673
00:42:53,926 --> 00:42:57,930
Those dolls were giving
a signal asking for help.

674
00:42:58,597 --> 00:43:01,642
But there was one more signal.

675
00:43:07,815 --> 00:43:12,361
The zipper on this suitcase
has a structure that doesn't catch easily.

676
00:43:12,444 --> 00:43:16,240
And yet, Samir…

677
00:43:27,334 --> 00:43:31,505
Mori said it caught her attention,
so we investigated.

678
00:43:39,930 --> 00:43:41,265
Take a look.

679
00:43:46,979 --> 00:43:48,605
The shape of his hand at this moment.

680
00:43:50,482 --> 00:43:51,817
A hand signal…

681
00:43:51,900 --> 00:43:54,361
-The same signal as those dolls.
-Yes.

682
00:43:54,987 --> 00:43:59,324
An internationally known signal.
The meaning of this hand signal is

683
00:44:00,367 --> 00:44:01,869
-"help".
-"Help."

684
00:44:02,995 --> 00:44:06,999
The one asking for help was Samir.

685
00:44:09,668 --> 00:44:11,545
We also established contact with Zafaria.

686
00:44:12,171 --> 00:44:14,715
This is your family.

687
00:44:14,798 --> 00:44:17,593
They were abducted by the organization
and brought to Japan, right?

688
00:44:17,676 --> 00:44:20,763
If anything happened to Lylea, the broker,

689
00:44:20,846 --> 00:44:22,306
your family would be in danger.

690
00:44:22,890 --> 00:44:24,892
That's why you couldn't
tell anyone, right?

691
00:44:25,517 --> 00:44:26,435
But it's okay now.

692
00:44:32,399 --> 00:44:34,985
-Why didn't you tell us?
-I'm very sorry!

693
00:44:35,486 --> 00:44:37,946
You were trying
to persuade Lylea at the time.

694
00:44:38,030 --> 00:44:40,866
Besides, when we tried to tell you,

695
00:44:40,949 --> 00:44:44,369
-Mori…
-Um…

696
00:44:44,953 --> 00:44:48,957
You got angry and said that
Customs should just stay out of it.

697
00:44:49,041 --> 00:44:52,419
So if you knew that I,
from Customs, had spoken up,

698
00:44:52,503 --> 00:44:54,505
I was sure you'd be angry again.

699
00:44:55,547 --> 00:44:59,885
So we decided not to tell you.

700
00:45:03,263 --> 00:45:05,641
Are you angry after all?

701
00:45:07,267 --> 00:45:09,478
He's not angry. Right, Hayami?

702
00:45:10,896 --> 00:45:12,272
Samir.

703
00:45:12,940 --> 00:45:13,857
First, I apologize.

704
00:45:15,067 --> 00:45:18,403
We could not stop your family from being

705
00:45:18,487 --> 00:45:20,447
brought into this country at the border.

706
00:45:21,573 --> 00:45:23,033
So that the same thing
never happens again,

707
00:45:23,116 --> 00:45:27,871
we will fulfill our duties
with even greater resolve.

708
00:45:31,959 --> 00:45:35,546
Your family is waiting.
Please go meet them.

709
00:45:51,311 --> 00:45:53,730
Welcome to Japan.

710
00:46:00,904 --> 00:46:02,990
Thank you.

711
00:46:55,292 --> 00:46:56,585
It really is far.

712
00:47:00,547 --> 00:47:01,590
Counselor.

713
00:47:03,467 --> 00:47:04,885
Good work today.

714
00:47:06,887 --> 00:47:11,391
Who on earth is that Machi Mori girl?

715
00:47:13,560 --> 00:47:16,647
Are you that frustrated
about being outsmarted?

716
00:47:18,023 --> 00:47:21,526
Well, she said it was
her first time in the field.

717
00:47:21,610 --> 00:47:23,737
I wondered why such a rookie
was put on this team.

718
00:47:24,696 --> 00:47:25,656
Because I put her in.

719
00:47:27,240 --> 00:47:28,241
Just kidding.

720
00:47:28,909 --> 00:47:30,619
An interesting girl, isn't she?

721
00:47:31,411 --> 00:47:32,788
I'm looking forward to what's to come.

722
00:47:44,341 --> 00:47:46,093
Machi! Hey!

723
00:47:46,968 --> 00:47:48,345
Chika!

724
00:47:49,346 --> 00:47:51,098
Take a seat, please.

725
00:47:51,807 --> 00:47:54,518
That was quite a tough day, huh?

726
00:47:54,601 --> 00:47:55,811
Right?

727
00:47:55,894 --> 00:47:57,479
Here you go.

728
00:47:59,064 --> 00:48:01,733
What a cute girl.
Is she a friend of yours, Chika?

729
00:48:01,817 --> 00:48:04,152
Yup. Eat up, Machi.

730
00:48:04,236 --> 00:48:06,780
The inari sushi here is the best in Japan.

731
00:48:06,863 --> 00:48:07,989
She's exaggerating.

732
00:48:08,073 --> 00:48:10,909
But the love put into it
is number one in the world.

733
00:48:10,992 --> 00:48:12,619
Thank you for the meal.

734
00:48:13,954 --> 00:48:15,622
Man, I'm really glad

735
00:48:15,706 --> 00:48:18,375
to be working at the same airport as you.

736
00:48:26,299 --> 00:48:28,510
Hey, why are you in Customs
in the first place?

737
00:48:28,593 --> 00:48:30,345
You didn't say a word about that.

738
00:48:32,431 --> 00:48:34,683
Because I like objects.

739
00:48:35,475 --> 00:48:36,852
I knew that much.

740
00:48:37,936 --> 00:48:39,354
And…

741
00:48:40,522 --> 00:48:41,606
Well, whatever.

742
00:48:43,024 --> 00:48:45,902
Here, eat up, eat up.

743
00:48:49,990 --> 00:48:52,909
-Oh my!
-Right?

744
00:48:52,993 --> 00:48:55,579
Hey, Ayako, she says it's great!

745
00:49:01,543 --> 00:49:03,712
MIDORI SUGIHARA
COUNSELOR OF BORDER CONTROL REFORM

746
00:49:13,889 --> 00:49:16,391
T-there's a bomb threat.

747
00:49:16,475 --> 00:49:19,811
<i>These 23 individuals</i>
<i>are subject to strict inspection.</i>

748
00:49:19,895 --> 00:49:23,482
<i>Why was tonight's flight to Rome targeted?</i>

749
00:49:23,565 --> 00:49:25,484
<i>-It's almost time.</i>
-Wait, Machi!

750
00:49:25,567 --> 00:49:26,443
What are you doing?

751
00:49:26,526 --> 00:49:27,569
Get down!

752
00:49:28,278 --> 00:49:29,571
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman

